(function(E){ const x = E["exam-11"] = E["exam-11"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x11-r1"] = {"id":"x11-r1","patterns":["RA-tech","GT1-ads","GT1-notices","PARA-cause","PARA-rules","TR-paraphrase","TR-hedge","TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords","TR-plural"],"title":{"en":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","tr":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","fa":"Reading ۱: متن ۱ (Passage 1) / بخش ۱ (Section 1)"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a technology passage by checking words such as rarely and no more than, and complete notes with one word that fits the gap exactly.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda bir teknoloji metninde rarely ve no more than gibi kelimeleri kontrol ederek TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar verebilecek, notları da boşluğa tam uyan tek bir kelimeyle tamamlayabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی در متنی درباره‌ی فناوری، با دقت به کلمه‌هایی مثل ⁨rarely⁩ و ⁨no more than⁩، بین ⁨TRUE⁩، ⁨FALSE⁩ و ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ تصمیم بگیری و یادداشت‌ها را با یک کلمه که دقیقاً با جای خالی جور است کامل کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"After this lesson, you can match details to six short notices and decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a community garden’s rules.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda ayrıntıları altı kısa duyuruyla eşleştirebilecek ve bir topluluk bahçesinin kuralları hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar verebileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی جزئیات را با شش اطلاعیه‌ی کوتاه جور کنی و درباره‌ی قانون‌های یک باغ محلی بین ⁨TRUE⁩، ⁨FALSE⁩ و ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ تصمیم بگیری."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 1: technology in the city","tr":"Reading Passage 1: şehirde teknoloji","fa":"Reading Passage 1: فناوری در شهر"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a technology passage by checking words such as rarely and no more than, and complete notes with one word that fits the gap exactly.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda bir teknoloji metninde rarely ve no more than gibi kelimeleri kontrol ederek TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar verebilecek, notları da boşluğa tam uyan tek bir kelimeyle tamamlayabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی در متنی درباره‌ی فناوری، با دقت به کلمه‌هایی مثل ⁨rarely⁩ و ⁨no more than⁩، بین ⁨TRUE⁩، ⁨FALSE⁩ و ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ تصمیم بگیری و یادداشت‌ها را با یک کلمه که دقیقاً با جای خالی جور است کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Words","tr":"Kelime","fa":"کلمه"},"value":"~900"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ زمینه"},"head":{"en":"This exam: farms on city rooftops","tr":"Bu sınav: şehirlerde çatı çiftlikleri","fa":"این آزمون: مزرعه‌های روی پشت‌بام‌های شهر"},"intro":{"en":"Technology and the way cities are built form a regular family of Academic topics. A Passage 1 on a technology usually moves in time order: where the idea came from, how it works today, then its benefits and its limits. Both question sets follow that order.","tr":"Teknoloji ve şehirlerin nasıl kurulduğu, sık görülen Academic konu ailelerinden biridir. Bir teknoloji üzerine Passage 1 genelde zaman sırasını izler: fikrin nereden çıktığı, bugün nasıl işlediği, sonra faydaları ve sınırları. İki soru grubu da bu sırayı takip eder.","fa":"فناوری و شیوه‌ی ساختن شهرها یکی از گروه‌های همیشگی موضوع‌های ⁨Academic⁩ است. ⁨Passage 1⁩ درباره‌ی یک فناوری معمولاً ترتیب زمانی دارد: ایده از کجا آمده، امروز چطور کار می‌کند و بعد فایده‌ها و محدودیت‌هایش. هر دو گروه سؤال همین ترتیب را دنبال می‌کنند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب در آن‌هاست"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x11-r1-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-tech","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-tech","n":18,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Food production on city roofs","tr":"Şehir çatılarında gıda üretimi","fa":"تولید غذا روی بام‌های شهر"},"asks":{"en":"A factual account of a technology on buildings: where the idea came from, the two main ways it works, what it offers cities and what holds it back. TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN covers the history and the methods; the notes cover the benefits and the limits.","tr":"Binalar üzerindeki bir teknolojiyi anlatan bilgilendirici bir metin: fikrin nereden çıktığı, iki temel çalışma şekli, şehirlere ne kazandırdığı ve önündeki engeller. TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN tarihi ve yöntemleri, notlar ise faydaları ve sınırları kapsar.","fa":"متنی اطلاعاتی درباره‌ی یک فناوری روی ساختمان‌ها: ایده از کجا آمده، دو روش اصلی کارش چیست، چه چیزی به شهرها می‌دهد و چه چیزی جلویش را می‌گیرد. ⁨TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN⁩ تاریخچه و روش‌ها را پوشش می‌دهد و یادداشت‌ها فایده‌ها و محدودیت‌ها را."},"fields":["Early roof gardens","Open-air farms","Rooftop greenhouses","Benefits","Weight and access","What can be grown"],"words":[{"a":"experts are uncertain","b":"historians still disagree about whether","tr":"uzmanlar emin değil","fa":"کارشناس‌ها مطمئن نیستند"},{"a":"mainly","b":"designed for ... rather than","tr":"esas olarak","fa":"بیشتر برای"},{"a":"hardly ever","b":"rarely / in only a few cases","tr":"neredeyse hiç","fa":"تقریباً هیچ‌وقت"},{"a":"less than half a metre","b":"no more than about 30 centimetres","tr":"yarım metreden az","fa":"کمتر از نیم متر"},{"a":"heated by","b":"warm air helps to heat","tr":"... ile ısıtılan","fa":"گرم‌شده با"},{"a":"all year round","b":"in every season / even in long winters","tr":"yıl boyunca","fa":"در تمام سال"},{"a":"take in","b":"absorb / soak up","tr":"emmek","fa":"جذب کردن"},{"a":"can carry the load","b":"is strong enough","tr":"yükü taşıyabilir","fa":"بار را تحمل می‌کند"},{"a":"too much space","b":"far larger areas","tr":"çok fazla alan","fa":"جای خیلی زیاد"},{"a":"staple foods","b":"basic foods eaten every day / grains","tr":"temel gıdalar","fa":"غذاهای اصلی"},{"a":"depend on","b":"survive only by / rely on","tr":"... -e bağlı olmak","fa":"وابسته بودن به"}],"traps":[{"en":"Frequency words decide the answer: if the text says something is hardly ever done, a statement that it is often done is FALSE, not NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Sıklık kelimeleri cevabı belirler: Metin bir şeyin neredeyse hiç yapılmadığını söylüyorsa, sık yapıldığını söyleyen ifade NOT GIVEN değil, FALSE’tur.","fa":"کلمه‌های بسامد جواب را تعیین می‌کنند: اگر متن بگوید کاری تقریباً هیچ‌وقت انجام نمی‌شود، جمله‌ای که می‌گوید اغلب انجام می‌شود ⁨FALSE⁩ است، نه ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩."},{"en":"A topic that is mentioned is not a point that is made: a text can mention school visits without saying what children learn from them. That is NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Söz edilen bir konu, söylenmiş bir bilgi demek değildir: Bir metin okul ziyaretlerinden söz edip çocukların bunlardan ne öğrendiğini hiç söylemeyebilir. Bu NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"اسم بردن از یک موضوع با گفتن نکته‌ای درباره‌اش فرق دارد: متن ممکن است از بازدید مدرسه‌ها حرف بزند، اما نگوید بچه‌ها از آن چه یاد می‌گیرند. این ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ است."},{"en":"Notes: read the words around the gap. After \"an\", the answer starts with a vowel sound; after \"within\" or \"several\", a plural noun usually follows.","tr":"Notlar: Boşluğun etrafındaki kelimeleri oku. \"An\"den sonra cevap ünlü bir sesle başlar; \"within\" ya da \"several\"dan sonra genelde çoğul bir isim gelir.","fa":"یادداشت‌ها: کلمه‌های دور جای خالی را بخوان. بعد از «⁨an⁩» جواب با صدای مصوت شروع می‌شود و بعد از «⁨within⁩» یا «⁨several⁩» معمولاً اسم جمع می‌آید."}],"example":{"text":"\"Green roofs are now required on new buildings in a handful of cities. Most cities still have no such rule.\"","item":"Statement: Most cities require green roofs on new buildings.","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Most cities still have no such rule\" contradicts \"most cities require\".","tr":"\"Çoğu şehirde hâlâ böyle bir kural yok\", \"çoğu şehir zorunlu tutuyor\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«بیشتر شهرها هنوز چنین قانونی ندارند» با «بیشتر شهرها الزامی کرده‌اند» تناقض دارد."}}},{"id":"RA-tech-proc","ctx":["RA-tech","RA-history"],"title":{"en":"Inventions, machines and buildings","tr":"İcatlar, makineler ve yapılar","fa":"اختراع‌ها، ماشین‌ها و سازه‌ها"},"asks":{"en":"How an invention, a machine or a building works, and how it was developed. Diagram labels name the parts; flow-charts follow how it works; sentences and short answers test purposes and materials.","tr":"Bir icadın, makinenin ya da yapının nasıl çalıştığı ve nasıl geliştirildiği. Diyagram etiketleri parçaları adlandırır; akış şemaları işleyişi izler; cümleler ve kısa cevaplar amaçları ve malzemeleri sınar.","fa":"اینکه یک اختراع، یک ماشین یا یک سازه چطور کار می‌کند و چطور توسعه یافت. برچسب‌های نمودار اسم قطعه‌ها را می‌خواهند؛ فلوچارت‌ها طرز کار را دنبال می‌کنند؛ جمله‌ها و جواب‌های کوتاه هدف و مواد را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["Diagram: warm air leaves through the ___","Flow-chart: water is pumped into the ___","Sentence: The first version was made of ___.","Short answer: Which material replaced wood?"],"words":[{"a":"part","b":"component","tr":"parça","fa":"قطعه"},{"a":"made of","b":"built from / constructed with","tr":"... -den yapılmış","fa":"ساخته‌شده از"},{"a":"purpose","b":"designed to / the aim was","tr":"amaç","fa":"هدف"},{"a":"runs on","b":"is powered by","tr":"... ile çalışır","fa":"با ... کار می‌کند"},{"a":"pass through","b":"flow through / circulate","tr":"içinden geçmek","fa":"عبور کردن از"},{"a":"opening","b":"gap / vent","tr":"açıklık","fa":"دریچه"},{"a":"cool","b":"lower the temperature","tr":"soğutmak","fa":"خنک کردن"},{"a":"heat up","b":"warm","tr":"ısıtmak","fa":"گرم کردن"},{"a":"improve","b":"make better / refine","tr":"geliştirmek","fa":"بهتر کردن"},{"a":"prototype","b":"first model / trial version","tr":"ilk örnek","fa":"نمونه‌ی اولیه"},{"a":"efficient","b":"wastes little energy","tr":"verimli","fa":"کارآمد"},{"a":"lightweight","b":"does not weigh much","tr":"hafif","fa":"سبک"}],"traps":[{"en":"Diagram labels: the text describes what a part does; the label needs its name.","tr":"Diyagram etiketleri: metin parçanın ne işe yaradığını anlatır; etiket onun adını ister.","fa":"برچسب نمودار: متن کار قطعه را توضیح می‌دهد؛ برچسب اسمش را می‌خواهد."},{"en":"Short answers: NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS. Copy a short noun phrase exactly; do not add words.","tr":"Kısa cevaplar: NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS. Kısa bir isim öbeğini aynen kopyala; kelime ekleme.","fa":"جواب کوتاه: NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS. یک گروه اسمی کوتاه را دقیقاً کپی کن؛ کلمه اضافه نکن."}],"example":{"text":"A solar oven is a simple box lined with foil. Sunlight passes through a glass lid and is reflected onto a black cooking pot, which absorbs the heat.","item":"Diagram: lid made of ___   (ONE WORD ONLY)","answer":"glass","why":{"en":"\"A glass lid\": the material is glass. Foil lines the box, not the lid.","tr":"\"Cam bir kapak\": malzeme cam. Folyo kapağı değil kutuyu kaplıyor.","fa":"«یک درِ شیشه‌ای»: جنسش شیشه است. فویل داخل جعبه است، نه روی در."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-tech","RA-history"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-tech","n":18,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Seven statements, then six notes","tr":"Yedi ifade, sonra altı not","fa":"هفت جمله، بعد شش یادداشت"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-7: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN. Questions 8-13: complete notes with ONE WORD ONLY from the passage. Both sets follow the order of the passage: the statements cover the history and the methods, the notes cover the benefits and the limits.","tr":"Soru 1-7: TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. Soru 8-13: notları metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla. İki grup da metnin sırasını izler: İfadeler tarihi ve yöntemleri, notlar faydaları ve sınırları kapsar.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۷: ⁨TRUE⁩، ⁨FALSE⁩ یا ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩. سؤال‌های ۸ تا ۱۳: یادداشت‌ها را فقط با یک کلمه از متن کامل کن. هر دو گروه به ترتیب متن‌اند: جمله‌ها تاریخچه و روش‌ها را پوشش می‌دهند و یادداشت‌ها فایده‌ها و محدودیت‌ها را."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Underline the subject of each statement (the gardens of Babylon, garden soil, greenhouses) and find the paragraph about it.","tr":"Her ifadenin öznesinin (Babil bahçeleri, bahçe toprağı, seralar) altını çiz ve onu anlatan paragrafı bul.","fa":"زیر فاعل هر جمله (باغ‌های بابل، خاک باغچه، گلخانه‌ها) خط بکش و پاراگرافی را که درباره‌ی آن است پیدا کن."},{"en":"Circle the words that limit the claim: rarely, usually, some, no more than, partly.","tr":"İddiayı sınırlayan kelimeleri daire içine al: rarely, usually, some, no more than, partly.","fa":"دور کلمه‌هایی که ادعا را محدود می‌کنند خط بکش: ⁨rarely⁩، ⁨usually⁩، ⁨some⁩، ⁨no more than⁩، ⁨partly⁩."},{"en":"Decide: the same meaning, a contradiction, or nothing about this point.","tr":"Karar ver: aynı anlam mı, bir çelişki mi, yoksa bu konuda hiçbir şey yok mu?","fa":"تصمیم بگیر: همان معنی است، تناقض دارد یا درباره‌ی این نکته هیچ چیزی گفته نشده."},{"en":"For the notes, find the paragraph from the heading, then copy one word in exactly the form you see, with its plural -s if it has one.","tr":"Notlar için başlıktan paragrafı bul, sonra tek kelimeyi gördüğün biçimiyle, varsa çoğul -s’siyle birlikte aynen kopyala.","fa":"برای یادداشت‌ها از روی عنوان پاراگراف را پیدا کن و بعد یک کلمه را دقیقاً به همان شکلی که می‌بینی کپی کن؛ اگر ⁨-s⁩ جمع دارد، آن را هم بنویس."}],"wrong":"Notes: the roof is covered with several protective layer","right":"Notes: the roof is covered with several protective layers","tip":{"en":"Why it works: a note answer is copied, so its form must match the passage too. After several, many or a number, English needs the plural -s. In Persian and Turkish the noun stays singular after these words, so the -s is easy to drop, and \"layer\" is marked wrong.","tr":"Neden işe yarar: Not cevabı kopyalanır, bu yüzden biçimi de metinle aynı olmalı. İngilizcede several, many ya da bir sayıdan sonra çoğul -s gerekir. Türkçede bu kelimelerden sonra isim tekil kalır (birkaç katman), bu yüzden -s’yi unutmak kolaydır ve \"layer\" yanlış sayılır.","fa":"این روش به کارت می‌آید، چون جواب یادداشت کپی می‌شود و شکلش هم باید با متن یکی باشد. در انگلیسی بعد از ⁨several⁩، ⁨many⁩ یا یک عدد، ⁨-s⁩ جمع لازم است. در فارسی بعد از این کلمه‌ها اسم مفرد می‌ماند («چند لایه»)، برای همین ⁨-s⁩ راحت جا می‌افتد و «⁨layer⁩» غلط حساب می‌شود."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Small words, different answers","tr":"Küçük kelimeler, farklı cevaplar","fa":"کلمه‌های کوچک، جواب‌های متفاوت"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The statement","Answer"],"tr":["Metin","İfade","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جمله","جواب"]},"rows":[["is hardly ever used","is usually used","FALSE"],["no more than 30 cm deep","less than half a metre deep","TRUE"],["some farms keep bees","most farms keep bees","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One statement, step by step","tr":"Bir ifade, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?","text":"\"The beehives on the hotel roof are inspected every ten days from April to September.\"","item":"Statement: In summer, the hives are checked more than once a month.","answer":"TRUE","walk":[{"en":"Find the place: \"inspected every ten days from April to September\".","tr":"Yeri bul: \"nisandan eylüle kadar on günde bir denetleniyor\".","fa":"جایش را پیدا کن: «از آوریل تا سپتامبر هر ده روز یک بار بازرسی می‌شوند»."},{"en":"Compare: every ten days is about three times a month, and summer is inside April to September.","tr":"Karşılaştır: On günde bir, ayda yaklaşık üç kez demektir; yaz da nisan ile eylül arasındadır.","fa":"مقایسه کن: هر ده روز یعنی تقریباً ماهی سه بار، و تابستان هم بین آوریل و سپتامبر است."},{"en":"Different words, same meaning: TRUE.","tr":"Kelimeler farklı, anlam aynı: TRUE.","fa":"کلمه‌ها فرق دارند، اما معنی یکی است: ⁨TRUE⁩."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Some city farms sell their salad to local restaurants.\" Statement: \"City farms earn most of their money from restaurants.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The text says some farms sell to restaurants, but not how much of their money comes from them.","tr":"Metin bazı çiftliklerin restoranlara sattığını söylüyor ama gelirlerinin ne kadarının buradan geldiğini söylemiyor.","fa":"متن می‌گوید بعضی مزرعه‌ها به رستوران‌ها می‌فروشند، اما نمی‌گوید چه مقدار از درآمدشان از آن‌جاست."}},"remember":{"en":"Circle the words that limit each claim, and copy every note answer in exactly the form of the passage. Result: you can now separate FALSE from NOT GIVEN in a technology passage and complete notes with the exact word.","tr":"Her iddiayı sınırlayan kelimeleri daire içine al ve her not cevabını metindeki biçimiyle aynen kopyala. Sonuç: Artık bir teknoloji metninde FALSE ile NOT GIVEN’ı ayırabilir, notları tam doğru kelimeyle tamamlayabilirsin.","fa":"دور کلمه‌هایی که هر ادعا را محدود می‌کنند خط بکش و جواب هر یادداشت را دقیقاً به همان شکلی که در متن آمده کپی کن. نتیجه: حالا می‌توانی در متنی درباره‌ی فناوری ⁨FALSE⁩ را از ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ جدا کنی و یادداشت‌ها را با همان کلمه‌ی دقیق کامل کنی."},"hook":{"en":"This Passage 1 follows a technology from its history to its limits. The main idea: small words such as rarely and no more than decide TRUE or FALSE.","tr":"Bu Passage 1 bir teknolojiyi tarihinden sınırlarına kadar izler. Ana fikir: TRUE ya da FALSE’u rarely ve no more than gibi küçük kelimeler belirler.","fa":"این ⁨Passage 1⁩ یک فناوری را از تاریخچه تا محدودیت‌هایش دنبال می‌کند. کلمه‌های کوچکی مثل ⁨rarely⁩ و ⁨no more than⁩ تعیین می‌کنند جواب ⁨TRUE⁩ باشد یا ⁨FALSE⁩."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x11-r1-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 1","title":{"en":"Farms above the streets","tr":"Sokakların üstündeki çiftlikler","fa":"مزرعه‌هایی بالای خیابان‌ها"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-tech"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.","passage":"Farms above the streets\n\nWalk through the centre of many large cities today and you may not realise that some of the salad on sale in local shops was grown a few floors above your head. Over the last fifteen years, farms on rooftops have spread from a handful of experiments to hundreds of sites around the world, from vegetable beds on top of apartment blocks to large commercial greenhouses. Supporters see them as a way of bringing food production back to the places where most people now live. Critics doubt that they will ever be more than a fashionable extra.\n\nThe idea of growing plants on roofs is far from new. Ancient writers described terraced gardens raised high above the city of Babylon, although historians still disagree about whether these gardens ever existed. In the late nineteenth century, gardens on the roofs of theatres and hotels became fashionable places to spend summer evenings in New York, but they were designed for entertainment rather than for growing food. In the 1920s, the Swiss-French architect Le Corbusier argued that the flat roofs made possible by reinforced concrete should be planted, so that a building would give back to the city the ground it had covered. Even so, food production on roofs remained rare until around 2010, when some of the first large commercial rooftop farms began operating in North American cities such as New York and Montreal.\n\nToday's rooftop farms fall broadly into two types. The first is the open-air farm, which looks much like a field that has been lifted onto a building. Before anything can be planted, the roof is covered with several protective layers: a waterproof sheet, a barrier that stops roots from pushing through it, and a drainage layer that allows excess water to run off. On top of these goes the growing medium. Ordinary garden soil is rarely used, because it becomes extremely heavy when it is wet. Instead, farmers use a lighter mixture of compost and small pieces of baked clay or volcanic rock, which is usually spread no more than about 30 centimetres deep.\n\nThe second type is the rooftop greenhouse. Here, plants are usually grown without any soil at all, using a method known as hydroponics: their roots hang in channels of water to which nutrients have been added, and the water is collected and used again. Because the system is enclosed, growers can control temperature, light and humidity, and they can produce crops all year round, even in cities with long, cold winters. Some greenhouses also benefit from the buildings underneath them. Warm air rising from the offices or warehouses below helps to heat the plants in winter, while the greenhouse itself adds a layer of insulation to the roof.\n\nSupporters point to a long list of benefits. Vegetables grown on a roof can reach a restaurant or shop within hours of being picked, so they can be sold fresher and with less packaging than food that has travelled for days by lorry. Plants and growing media also absorb rain, which reduces the amount of water rushing into city drains during heavy storms. In summer, a planted roof stays far cooler than a bare one, keeping the rooms beneath it cooler too. Some farms keep beehives, and many run classes for local schools, giving children who have only seen vegetables in supermarkets the chance to watch them grow.\n\nYet rooftop farming faces serious limits. The most basic is weight. A layer of wet growing medium, together with the plants, the water and the people working on it, places a heavy load on a roof, and many older buildings were never designed to carry one. Before a farm can be built, an engineer must check that the structure is strong enough, and the cost of strengthening a roof is so high that many projects end at this stage. Access is a further problem: compost, tools and harvested crops all have to be carried up and down, often in a lift that is shared with the building's other users.\n\nThere are also limits to what can be grown. Rooftop farms are best suited to crops that grow quickly, take up little space and sell for a high price, such as salad leaves, herbs and tomatoes. Staple foods such as wheat and rice need far larger areas, and growing them on roofs would make little economic sense. As a result, even enthusiastic supporters accept that roofs will never feed a whole city. Studies that have measured the roof space available in particular cities suggest that rooftop farms could meet a useful part of local demand for certain vegetables, but only a tiny proportion of people's total food needs. Many farms also survive financially only by adding other sources of income, such as hosting events, charging for educational visits or selling directly to expensive restaurants.\n\nFor these reasons, some researchers argue that the real value of rooftop farms lies less in the amount of food they produce than in what they do for cities in other ways: cooling buildings, reducing the risk of flooding and reconnecting people with the origins of what they eat. Others are more optimistic, pointing to new lightweight growing systems and to the rising number of city governments that require some new buildings to have planted roofs. Whichever view proves correct, the view from many office windows is likely to include rather more vegetables in the future.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 1-7. Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Experts are uncertain whether the gardens of Babylon really existed.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"historians still disagree about whether these gardens ever existed","why":{"en":"\"Historians still disagree about whether these gardens ever existed\": experts = historians, uncertain = still disagree.","tr":"\"Tarihçiler bu bahçelerin gerçekten var olup olmadığı konusunda hâlâ anlaşamıyor\": experts = historians.","fa":"«تاریخ‌دان‌ها هنوز بر سر اینکه این باغ‌ها اصلاً وجود داشته‌اند یا نه توافق ندارند»: ⁨experts⁩ یعنی ⁨historians⁩."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-hedge"]},{"n":2,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The roof gardens of nineteenth-century New York were mainly used for growing food.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"they were designed for entertainment rather than for growing food","why":{"en":"They \"were designed for entertainment rather than for growing food\".","tr":"Bunlar \"yiyecek yetiştirmek için değil, eğlence için tasarlanmıştı\".","fa":"این باغ‌ها «برای سرگرمی طراحی شده بودند، نه برای پرورش غذا»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":3,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Most architects of the 1920s rejected Le Corbusier's ideas about roofs.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"Le Corbusier argued that the flat roofs made possible by reinforced concrete should be planted","why":{"en":"The text gives Le Corbusier's argument, but says nothing about how other architects reacted to it.","tr":"Metin Le Corbusier’nin görüşünü veriyor ama diğer mimarların buna nasıl tepki verdiğinden hiç söz etmiyor.","fa":"متن نظر لوکوربوزیه را می‌آورد، اما هیچ حرفی از واکنش معمارهای دیگر نمی‌زند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords"]},{"n":4,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Open-air rooftop farms usually use ordinary garden soil.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"Ordinary garden soil is rarely used","why":{"en":"\"Ordinary garden soil is rarely used\" contradicts \"usually use\"; it is too heavy when wet.","tr":"\"Sıradan bahçe toprağı nadiren kullanılır\", \"genellikle kullanılır\" ile çelişiyor; ıslakken çok ağırdır.","fa":"«خاک معمولی باغچه به‌ندرت استفاده می‌شود» با «معمولاً استفاده می‌شود» تناقض دارد؛ این خاک وقتی خیس است خیلی سنگین می‌شود."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":5,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The growing medium on an open-air farm is normally less than half a metre deep.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"usually spread no more than about 30 centimetres deep","why":{"en":"\"Usually... no more than about 30 centimetres deep\": 30 cm is less than half a metre.","tr":"\"Genellikle... en fazla yaklaşık 30 santimetre derinlikte\": 30 cm yarım metreden azdır.","fa":"«معمولاً... حداکثر حدود ۳۰ سانتی‌متر عمق»: ۳۰ سانتی‌متر کمتر از نیم متر است."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":6,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Some rooftop greenhouses are partly heated by the building underneath.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"Warm air rising from the offices or warehouses below helps to heat the plants in winter","why":{"en":"\"Warm air rising from the offices or warehouses below helps to heat the plants\": partly heated = helps to heat.","tr":"\"Alttaki ofislerden ya da depolardan yükselen sıcak hava bitkileri ısıtmaya yardım ediyor\": partly heated = helps to heat.","fa":"«هوای گرمی که از دفترها یا انبارهای طبقه‌ی پایین بالا می‌آید به گرم شدن گیاه‌ها کمک می‌کند»: ⁨partly heated⁩ یعنی ⁨helps to heat⁩."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":7,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Children who visit rooftop farms eat more vegetables afterwards.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"many run classes for local schools","why":{"en":"Farms run classes for schools, but the text says nothing about what children eat afterwards.","tr":"Çiftlikler okullar için dersler düzenliyor ama metin çocukların sonra ne yediğinden hiç söz etmiyor.","fa":"مزرعه‌ها برای مدرسه‌ها کلاس می‌گذارند، اما متن درباره‌ی اینکه بچه‌ها بعدش چه می‌خورند چیزی نمی‌گوید."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 8-13. Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"note","notesTitle":"Rooftop farms: benefits and limits","questions":[{"n":8,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Benefits · vegetables can reach shops within ___ of being picked","accept":["hours"],"limit":1,"evidence":"within hours of being picked","why":{"en":"\"Within hours of being picked\". Plural: \"hour\" is wrong.","tr":"\"Toplandıktan sonraki birkaç saat içinde\". Çoğul: \"hour\" yanlış olur.","fa":"«ظرف چند ساعت بعد از چیده شدن». جمع است: «⁨hour⁩» غلط است."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":9,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Benefits · produce needs less ___ than food that travels far","accept":["packaging"],"limit":1,"evidence":"sold fresher and with less packaging","why":{"en":"\"Sold fresher and with less packaging than food that has travelled for days by lorry\".","tr":"\"Günlerce kamyonla yol yapmış yiyecekten daha taze ve daha az ambalajla satılabilir\".","fa":"«تازه‌تر و با بسته‌بندی کمتر از غذایی که روزها با کامیون در راه بوده فروخته می‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":10,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Benefits · plants and growing media take in ___, so less water flows into drains","accept":["rain"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Plants and growing media also absorb rain","why":{"en":"\"Absorb rain, which reduces the amount of water rushing into city drains\": take in = absorb.","tr":"\"Yağmuru emer, bu da şehrin yağmur suyu kanallarına akan suyu azaltır\": take in = absorb.","fa":"«باران را جذب می‌کنند و همین آبی را که به آب‌روهای شهر سرازیر می‌شود کم می‌کند»: ⁨take in⁩ یعنی ⁨absorb⁩."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":11,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Limits · an ___ must check that the roof can carry the load","accept":["engineer"],"limit":1,"evidence":"an engineer must check that the structure is strong enough","why":{"en":"\"An engineer must check that the structure is strong enough\". \"An\" tells you the word starts with a vowel sound.","tr":"\"Bir mühendis yapının yeterince sağlam olduğunu kontrol etmeli\". \"An\", kelimenin ünlü bir sesle başladığını gösterir.","fa":"«یک مهندس باید بررسی کند که سازه به‌قدر کافی محکم باشد». «⁨an⁩» نشان می‌دهد کلمه با صدای مصوت شروع می‌شود."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Limits · staple foods such as wheat and ___ need too much space","accept":["rice"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Staple foods such as wheat and rice need far larger areas","why":{"en":"\"Staple foods such as wheat and rice need far larger areas\": too much space = far larger areas.","tr":"\"Buğday ve pirinç gibi temel gıdalar çok daha geniş alanlara ihtiyaç duyar\": too much space = far larger areas.","fa":"«غذاهای اصلی مثل گندم و برنج به زمین‌های خیلی بزرگ‌تری نیاز دارند»: ⁨too much space⁩ یعنی ⁨far larger areas⁩."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Limits · many farms depend on other sources of ___","accept":["income"],"limit":1,"evidence":"adding other sources of income","why":{"en":"\"Survive financially only by adding other sources of income\": depend on = survive only by.","tr":"\"Ancak başka gelir kaynakları ekleyerek mali açıdan ayakta kalabiliyorlar\": depend on = survive only by.","fa":"«فقط با اضافه کردن منبع‌های درآمد دیگر از نظر مالی سر پا می‌مانند»: ⁨depend on⁩ یعنی ⁨survive only by⁩."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]}],"id":"c-x11-r1-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Staple foods such as wheat and rice need far larger areas.\" Staple foods are...","options":["basic foods that people eat every day","foods sold at high prices","foods grown only in greenhouses"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Staple foods = the basic foods most people eat regularly, such as bread or rice.","tr":"Staple foods = çoğu insanın düzenli olarak yediği temel gıdalar; ekmek ya da pirinç gibi.","fa":"⁨staple foods⁩ یعنی غذاهای اصلی که بیشتر مردم مرتب می‌خورند، مثل نان یا برنج."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A statement says \"less than half a metre deep\". Which phrase in a passage could mean the same?","options":["at least a metre deep","no more than about 30 centimetres deep","deeper than ordinary soil"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"30 cm is less than half a metre, so \"no more than about 30 centimetres\" matches.","tr":"30 cm yarım metreden azdır; bu yüzden \"en fazla yaklaşık 30 santimetre\" uyar.","fa":"۳۰ سانتی‌متر کمتر از نیم متر است، پس «حداکثر حدود ۳۰ سانتی‌متر» جور است."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"A note reads \"an ___ must check the roof\". What does \"an\" tell you about the answer?","options":["it is a plural noun","it starts with a vowel sound","it is a number"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"An\" comes before a vowel sound: an engineer, an expert.","tr":"\"An\" ünlü bir sesten önce gelir: an engineer, an expert.","fa":"«⁨an⁩» قبل از صدای مصوت می‌آید: ⁨an engineer⁩، ⁨an expert⁩."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Some rooftop farms keep beehives.\" Statement: \"Most rooftop farms keep beehives.\"","options":["TRUE","NOT GIVEN","FALSE"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"Some\" does not tell you how many; the text gives no information about \"most\".","tr":"\"Some\" kaç tane olduğunu söylemez; metin \"most\" hakkında bilgi vermiyor.","fa":"«⁨some⁩» نمی‌گوید چندتا؛ متن درباره‌ی «⁨most⁩» اطلاعاتی نمی‌دهد."}}],"id":"c-x11-r1-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r1"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 1: notices and garden rules","tr":"GT Reading Section 1: duyurular ve bahçe kuralları","fa":"GT Reading Section 1: اطلاعیه‌ها و قانون‌های یک باغ"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can match details to six short notices and decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a community garden’s rules.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda ayrıntıları altı kısa duyuruyla eşleştirebilecek ve bir topluluk bahçesinin kuralları hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar verebileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی جزئیات را با شش اطلاعیه‌ی کوتاه جور کنی و درباره‌ی قانون‌های یک باغ محلی بین ⁨TRUE⁩، ⁨FALSE⁩ و ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ تصمیم بگیری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"about 20 min","tr":"yaklaşık 20 dk","fa":"حدود ۲۰ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ زمینه"},"head":{"en":"This exam: an allotment noticeboard and a community garden","tr":"Bu sınav: bir hobi bahçesi ilan panosu ve bir topluluk bahçesi","fa":"این آزمون: تابلوی اعلانات قطعه‌زمین‌های اجاره‌ای و یک باغ محلی"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 1 often puts a set of short notices or adverts next to a longer information sheet. The short texts test quick matching; the information sheet tests rules, times, prices and exceptions.","tr":"GT Section 1 çoğu zaman bir dizi kısa duyuru ya da ilanı daha uzun bir bilgi metninin yanına koyar. Kısa metinler hızlı eşleştirmeyi, bilgi metni ise kuralları, saatleri, fiyatları ve istisnaları ölçer.","fa":"⁨GT Section 1⁩ اغلب چند اطلاعیه یا آگهی کوتاه را کنار یک برگه‌ی اطلاعات بلندتر می‌گذارد. متن‌های کوتاه جور کردن سریع را می‌سنجند و برگه‌ی اطلاعات قانون‌ها، ساعت‌ها، قیمت‌ها و استثناها را."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب در آن‌هاست"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x11-r1gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT1-ads","GT1-notices","PARA-rules"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-ads","n":24,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 24 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 24’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۴ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"An allotment noticeboard and a garden's rules","tr":"Bir hobi bahçesi ilan panosu ve bir bahçenin kuralları","fa":"تابلوی اعلانات قطعه‌زمین‌ها و قانون‌های یک باغ"},"asks":{"en":"First, six short notices, A-F, from the noticeboard of a site where people rent plots to grow food: you match each piece of information to one notice. Then a community garden's information for new members: membership, shared beds, work days, tools and what is not allowed. You decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Önce, insanların yiyecek yetiştirmek için parsel kiraladığı bir alanın ilan panosundan A-F harfli altı kısa duyuru: Her bilgiyi bir duyuruyla eşleştiriyorsun. Sonra bir topluluk bahçesinin yeni üyeler için bilgileri: üyelik, ortak tarhlar, çalışma günleri, aletler ve yasak olanlar. TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar veriyorsun.","fa":"اول شش اطلاعیه‌ی کوتاه با حرف ⁨A⁩ تا ⁨F⁩ از تابلوی اعلانات جایی که مردم قطعه‌زمین اجاره می‌کنند تا سبزی و میوه بکارند: هر نکته را با یکی از اطلاعیه‌ها جور می‌کنی. بعد اطلاعات یک باغ محلی برای عضوهای تازه: عضویت، کرت‌های مشترک، روزهای کار گروهی، ابزارها و کارهای ممنوع. بین ⁨TRUE⁩، ⁨FALSE⁩ و ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ تصمیم می‌گیری."},"fields":["Seed swap","Water","Plot to share","Tool library","Workshops","Bonfires","Membership","Shared beds","Work days","Not allowed"],"words":[{"a":"people living nearby","b":"the houses along the lane / neighbours","tr":"yakında oturanlar","fa":"کسانی که نزدیک زندگی می‌کنند"},{"a":"far higher than expected","b":"more than twice what we expected","tr":"beklenenden çok daha yüksek","fa":"خیلی بیشتر از حد انتظار"},{"a":"look after","b":"manage / take care of","tr":"bakmak, ilgilenmek","fa":"رسیدگی کردن"},{"a":"with their names on","b":"labelled","tr":"üzerinde adı yazılı","fa":"با اسمی که رویش نوشته شده"},{"a":"borrow","b":"take for a few days and bring back","tr":"ödünç almak","fa":"قرض گرفتن"},{"a":"what to wear","b":"old clothes and boots","tr":"ne giyileceği","fa":"چه بپوشی"},{"a":"get rid of","b":"take to the recycling centre / throw away","tr":"atmak, -den kurtulmak","fa":"دور ریختن"},{"a":"reduced fee","b":"a lower price for some groups","tr":"indirimli ücret","fa":"هزینه‌ی کمتر"},{"a":"given away","b":"passed on to the food bank","tr":"bağışlanmış","fa":"اهداشده"},{"a":"accompanied by","b":"with an adult at all times","tr":"... eşliğinde","fa":"همراهِ"},{"a":"allocated","b":"given out to members","tr":"dağıtılmış","fa":"تقسیم‌شده"},{"a":"may not leave the garden","b":"must not be taken out of the garden","tr":"bahçeden çıkarılamaz","fa":"نباید از باغ بیرون برده شود"}],"traps":[{"en":"Several notices mention money: a rent, a deposit, a price. Match the exact idea in the question, not just the topic.","tr":"Birkaç duyuru paradan söz ediyor: kira, depozito, fiyat. Yalnızca konuyu değil, sorudaki fikrin tam kendisini eşleştir.","fa":"چند اطلاعیه از پول حرف می‌زنند: اجاره، ودیعه، قیمت. خود ایده‌ی سؤال را دقیق جور کن، نه فقط موضوع را."},{"en":"Exceptions change the answer: if a rule says \"not allowed, except...\", a statement about \"all\" or \"any\" is FALSE.","tr":"İstisnalar cevabı değiştirir: Bir kural \"yasak, ... hariç\" diyorsa \"hepsi\" ya da \"hiçbiri\" diyen bir ifade FALSE’tur.","fa":"استثناها جواب را عوض می‌کنند: اگر قانونی بگوید «ممنوع است، به‌جز...»، جمله‌ای درباره‌ی «همه» یا «هیچ‌کدام» ⁨FALSE⁩ است."}],"example":{"text":"Notice: \"The car park is for plot holders only, except on open days, when visitors may use it.\"","item":"Statement: Visitors can never use the car park.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Except on open days, when visitors may use it\" contradicts \"never\".","tr":"\"Açık günler hariç; o günlerde ziyaretçiler de kullanabilir\", \"asla\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«به‌جز روزهای بازدید عمومی که بازدیدکننده‌ها هم می‌توانند از آن استفاده کنند» با «هرگز» تناقض دارد."}}},{"id":"GT1-ads","ctx":["GT1-ads"],"title":{"en":"Adverts and listings","tr":"İlanlar ve listeler","fa":"آگهی‌ها و فهرست‌ها"},"asks":{"en":"Short adverts or listings A-F for courses, events, campsites, tours or clubs. Questions ask which advert mentions a fact, or whether a statement is TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Kurslar, etkinlikler, kamp alanları, turlar ya da kulüpler için A-F harfli kısa ilanlar veya listeler. Sorular hangi ilanın bir bilgiden söz ettiğini ya da bir ifadenin TRUE, FALSE veya NOT GIVEN olduğunu sorar.","fa":"آگهی‌ها یا فهرست‌های کوتاه A تا F برای کلاس‌ها، رویدادها، کمپ‌ها، تورها یا باشگاه‌ها. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند کدام آگهی به یک نکته اشاره می‌کند، یا یک جمله TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN است."},"fields":["Which course is suitable for complete beginners?","Which event takes place outdoors?","Which campsite allows dogs?","Booking is required for all tours."],"words":[{"a":"suitable for beginners","b":"no experience needed","tr":"yeni başlayanlara uygun","fa":"مناسب مبتدی‌ها"},{"a":"free of charge","b":"at no cost / complimentary","tr":"ücretsiz","fa":"رایگان"},{"a":"booking essential","b":"places must be reserved","tr":"rezervasyon şart","fa":"رزرو الزامی"},{"a":"reduced price","b":"discount / 20% off","tr":"indirimli fiyat","fa":"قیمت با تخفیف"},{"a":"family-friendly","b":"children welcome","tr":"aileye uygun","fa":"مناسب خانواده"},{"a":"outdoors","b":"in the open air","tr":"açık havada","fa":"در فضای باز"},{"a":"pets allowed","b":"dogs welcome","tr":"evcil hayvan kabul edilir","fa":"ورود حیوان خانگی آزاد"},{"a":"on site","b":"at the campsite itself","tr":"tesis içinde","fa":"در خود محل"},{"a":"equipment provided","b":"everything supplied","tr":"ekipman sağlanır","fa":"تجهیزات داده می‌شود"},{"a":"refundable","b":"money back if you cancel","tr":"iade edilebilir","fa":"قابل استرداد"},{"a":"weekly","b":"once a week","tr":"haftalık","fa":"هفتگی"},{"a":"within walking distance","b":"nearby / a short walk away","tr":"yürüme mesafesinde","fa":"با پای پیاده نزدیک"}],"traps":[{"en":"Matching: two adverts mention dogs, but only one allows them. Read the whole line.","tr":"Eşleştirme: iki ilan köpeklerden söz eder ama yalnızca biri izin verir. Satırın tamamını oku.","fa":"جورکردن: دو آگهی از سگ حرف می‌زنند، ولی فقط یکی اجازه می‌دهد. کل خط را بخوان."},{"en":"\"Free\" in one advert may mean free parking, not free entry.","tr":"Bir ilandaki \"free\" giriş değil, ücretsiz otopark anlamına gelebilir.","fa":"«free» در یک آگهی شاید یعنی پارکینگ رایگان، نه ورود رایگان."}],"example":{"text":"C  Lakeside Campsite. Quiet site by the water. Sorry, no dogs. Shop on site.\nD  Hilltop Farm Camping. Families and well-behaved pets welcome. Nearest shop 2 km.","item":"Which campsite allows dogs?","answer":"D","why":{"en":"Both mention dogs or pets. C says \"no dogs\"; D says \"pets welcome\".","tr":"İkisi de köpek ya da evcil hayvandan söz ediyor. C \"köpek yok\", D \"evcil hayvanlar kabul\" diyor.","fa":"هر دو از سگ یا حیوان خانگی حرف می‌زنند. C می‌گوید «سگ ممنوع»؛ D می‌گوید «حیوان خانگی پذیرفته می‌شود»."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-ads"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-ads","n":24,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 24 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 24’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۴ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}},{"id":"GT1-notices","ctx":["GT1-notices"],"title":{"en":"Notices, rules and FAQs","tr":"Duyurular, kurallar ve SSS","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول"},"asks":{"en":"Notices, rules and frequently asked questions for a service: a tram, a leisure centre, a block of flats, a competition. Questions test rules, conditions, dates and exceptions.","tr":"Bir hizmet için duyurular, kurallar ve sık sorulan sorular: tramvay, spor merkezi, apartman, yarışma. Sorular kuralları, koşulları, tarihleri ve istisnaları sınar.","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول برای یک خدمت: تراموا، مرکز ورزشی، یک ساختمان مسکونی، یک مسابقه. سؤال‌ها قانون‌ها، شرط‌ها، تاریخ‌ها و استثناها را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["Passengers must buy a ticket before boarding.","Children under five travel free.","Refunds are given for delays of over 30 minutes.","Residents may leave bicycles in the hallway."],"words":[{"a":"must","b":"are required to","tr":"zorunda","fa":"باید"},{"a":"not allowed","b":"prohibited / not permitted","tr":"yasak","fa":"ممنوع"},{"a":"within 14 days","b":"in less than two weeks","tr":"14 gün içinde","fa":"ظرف ۱۴ روز"},{"a":"can claim","b":"are entitled to / are eligible for","tr":"talep edebilir","fa":"می‌تواند درخواست کند"},{"a":"apply","b":"submit a form","tr":"başvurmak","fa":"درخواست دادن"},{"a":"proof","b":"a receipt / evidence of","tr":"kanıt","fa":"مدرک"},{"a":"residents","b":"people living in the building","tr":"sakinler","fa":"ساکنان"},{"a":"compensation","b":"money for a problem you had","tr":"tazminat","fa":"غرامت"},{"a":"beforehand","b":"in advance","tr":"önceden","fa":"از قبل"},{"a":"except","b":"apart from / with the exception of","tr":"hariç","fa":"به‌جز"},{"a":"responsible for","b":"must take care of","tr":"... -den sorumlu","fa":"مسئولِ"},{"a":"on request","b":"if you ask","tr":"talep üzerine","fa":"در صورت درخواست"}],"traps":[{"en":"Exceptions: \"all passengers must..., except season-ticket holders\". A statement about everyone may be FALSE.","tr":"İstisnalar: \"bütün yolcular ... zorunda, abonman sahipleri hariç\". Herkes hakkındaki bir ifade FALSE olabilir.","fa":"استثناها: «همه‌ی مسافران باید...، به‌جز دارندگان بلیت فصلی». جمله‌ای درباره‌ی همه ممکن است FALSE باشد."},{"en":"Numbers in conditions: \"30 minutes or more\" and \"over 30 minutes\" are not the same.","tr":"Koşullardaki sayılar: \"30 dakika veya daha fazla\" ile \"30 dakikadan fazla\" aynı değildir.","fa":"عددها در شرط‌ها: «۳۰ دقیقه یا بیشتر» با «بیش از ۳۰ دقیقه» یکی نیست."}],"example":{"text":"Delay Repay: if your train arrives 30 minutes or more late, you can claim 50% of your ticket price. Claims must be made within 28 days of travel.","item":"Statement: Passengers can claim the full price of their ticket.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"The notice says 50%, which contradicts \"the full price\".","tr":"Duyuru %50 diyor; bu \"tam fiyat\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"اطلاعیه می‌گوید ۵۰٪، که با «قیمت کامل» در تضاد است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-notices"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-notices","n":22,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 22 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 22’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۲ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Seven questions, then seven statements","tr":"Yedi soru, sonra yedi ifade","fa":"هفت سؤال، بعد هفت جمله"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-7: which notice, A-F, contains each piece of information. There are seven questions and six notices, so at least one letter is used twice. Questions 8-14: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on the garden's information for new members.","tr":"Soru 1-7: Her bilgi hangi duyuruda (A-F)? Yedi soru ve altı duyuru var, yani en az bir harf iki kez kullanılır. Soru 8-14: bahçenin yeni üyeler için bilgileri hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۷: هر نکته در کدام اطلاعیه (⁨A⁩ تا ⁨F⁩) است. هفت سؤال و شش اطلاعیه داریم، پس دست‌کم یک حرف دو بار می‌آید. سؤال‌های ۸ تا ۱۴: ⁨TRUE⁩، ⁨FALSE⁩ یا ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ درباره‌ی اطلاعات باغ برای عضوهای تازه."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the seven questions first and decide what each one needs: a reason, a rule, a limit, a piece of advice.","tr":"Önce yedi soruyu oku ve her birinin ne istediğine karar ver: bir neden, bir kural, bir sınır, bir tavsiye.","fa":"اول هفت سؤال را بخوان و ببین هر کدام چه می‌خواهد: یک دلیل، یک قانون، یک محدودیت یا یک توصیه."},{"en":"Scan the notices for that idea, not for the same words, and check the whole sentence.","tr":"Duyurularda aynı kelimeleri değil o fikri ara ve cümlenin tamamını kontrol et.","fa":"در اطلاعیه‌ها دنبال همان ایده بگرد، نه همان کلمه‌ها، و کل جمله را بررسی کن."},{"en":"For the information sheet, use the headings (Membership, Work days, Tools) to find each statement's place.","tr":"Bilgi metninde her ifadenin yerini bulmak için başlıkları (Membership, Work days, Tools) kullan.","fa":"برای برگه‌ی اطلاعات با کمک عنوان‌ها (⁨Membership⁩، ⁨Work days⁩، ⁨Tools⁩) جای هر جمله را پیدا کن."},{"en":"Answer FALSE only when the text says the opposite; if it says nothing, the answer is NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Yalnızca metin tersini söylüyorsa FALSE de; hiçbir şey söylemiyorsa cevap NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"فقط وقتی ⁨FALSE⁩ بزن که متن خلافش را بگوید؛ اگر چیزی نگوید، جواب ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ است."}],"wrong":"The rules say nothing about parking, so the answer is FALSE.","right":"The rules say nothing about parking, so the answer is NOT GIVEN.","tip":{"en":"Why it works: FALSE needs a sentence in the text that clashes with the statement. In everyday thinking, \"not said\" can feel like \"not true\", but in this test a text that says nothing always gives NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Neden işe yarar: FALSE için metinde ifadeyle çelişen bir cümle gerekir. Günlük düşüncede \"söylenmemiş\" olan \"doğru değil\" gibi gelebilir ama bu sınavda metin bir konuda hiçbir şey söylemiyorsa cevap her zaman NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"این روش به کارت می‌آید، چون برای ⁨FALSE⁩ باید جمله‌ای در متن باشد که با جمله‌ی سؤال تناقض داشته باشد. در فکر روزمره «گفته نشده» ممکن است شبیه «درست نیست» به نظر برسد، اما در این آزمون وقتی متن درباره‌ی چیزی ساکت است، جواب همیشه ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ است."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Rules with conditions","tr":"Koşullu kurallar","fa":"قانون‌های شرط‌دار"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The rules","The statement","Answer"],"tr":["Kurallar","İfade","Cevap"],"fa":["قانون‌ها","جمله","جواب"]},"rows":[["no cycling, except on the main path","cycling is not allowed anywhere","FALSE"],["come to at least one meeting a month","come to every meeting","FALSE"],["refreshments are served","refreshments are free","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One notice, step by step","tr":"Bir duyuru, adım adım","fa":"یک اطلاعیه، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Which notice mentions the following?","text":"A \"Coffee mornings are free, but please bring your own cup.\" B \"Free parking is available behind the hall for all visitors.\"","item":"Information: something you need to take with you","answer":"A","walk":[{"en":"The idea: something you must take with you.","tr":"Fikir: yanında götürmen gereken bir şey.","fa":"ایده: چیزی که باید با خودت ببری."},{"en":"B also says \"free\", but nothing has to be taken.","tr":"B de \"free\" diyor ama yanında bir şey götürmen gerekmiyor.","fa":"در ⁨B⁩ هم «⁨free⁩» آمده، اما لازم نیست چیزی با خودت ببری."},{"en":"A: \"please bring your own cup\" = something to take: A.","tr":"A: \"lütfen kendi bardağını getir\" = götürülecek bir şey: A.","fa":"⁨A⁩: «لطفاً لیوان خودت را بیاور» یعنی چیزی که باید ببری: ⁨A⁩."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Visitors must sign in at reception.\" Statement: \"Visitors must show a passport at reception.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Signing in is required, but the text says nothing about a passport.","tr":"Girişte kayıt yaptırmak gerekli ama metin pasaporttan hiç söz etmiyor.","fa":"ثبت ورود لازم است، اما متن هیچ حرفی از پاسپورت نمی‌زند."}},"remember":{"en":"Match the idea in each question, not the words, and answer FALSE only when the text says the opposite. Result: you can now match details to short notices quickly and keep FALSE and NOT GIVEN apart.","tr":"Her sorudaki kelimeleri değil fikri eşleştir; yalnızca metin tersini söylediğinde FALSE de. Sonuç: Artık ayrıntıları kısa duyurularla hızla eşleştirebilir, FALSE ile NOT GIVEN’ı birbirinden ayırabilirsin.","fa":"ایده‌ی هر سؤال را جور کن، نه کلمه‌هایش را، و فقط وقتی ⁨FALSE⁩ بزن که متن خلافش را بگوید. نتیجه: حالا می‌توانی جزئیات را سریع با اطلاعیه‌های کوتاه جور کنی و ⁨FALSE⁩ و ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ را از هم جدا نگه داری."},"hook":{"en":"Section 1 here is a noticeboard and a garden's rules. The main idea: match the idea, not the words, and keep FALSE for a real contradiction.","tr":"Buradaki Section 1 bir ilan panosu ve bir bahçenin kurallarıdır. Ana fikir: Kelimeleri değil fikri eşleştir; FALSE’u gerçek bir çelişki için sakla.","fa":"این ⁨Section 1⁩ یک تابلوی اعلانات و قانون‌های یک باغ است. ایده را جور کن، نه کلمه‌ها را، و ⁨FALSE⁩ را فقط برای تناقض واقعی نگه دار."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x11-r1-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 1","title":{"en":"An allotment noticeboard and a community garden","tr":"Bir hobi bahçesi ilan panosu ve bir topluluk bahçesi","fa":"تابلوی اعلانات قطعه‌زمین‌ها و یک باغ محلی"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT1-ads","GT1-notices"],"texts":[{"title":"Ashgrove Allotments: on the noticeboard this month","kind":"notices","body":"A  Seed swap\nBring any seeds left over from last year to the meeting room on Saturday 8 March, between 10 am and 12 noon, and take home something new to try. All seeds should be in envelopes labelled with the name of the plant and the year they were collected. Tea and cake will be served, and entry is free.\n\nB  Water: please read\nFrom 1 June, the taps on the site will only be turned on between 6 and 9 am and between 6 and 9 pm. Last summer, our water bill was more than twice what we had expected, and we cannot afford a repeat. Hoses may not be left running at any time. The committee has a few spare water butts for collecting rain, at £5 each.\n\nC  Half plot to share\nI have a full plot near the main gate, but since my knee operation I can no longer manage all of it. I am looking for someone to take over the half nearest the path, which has a small shed and two fruit bushes. You would pay half of the annual rent. Experience is not essential. Please call Rita on 07700 900412.\n\nD  Tool library\nThe tool library in the old shed by the car park is now open on Sunday mornings from 9 to 11. Plot holders can borrow larger tools, such as a rotavator or a hedge trimmer, for up to three days at a time. There is no charge, but a deposit of £20 is needed for anything with an engine. Please clean tools before you return them.\n\nE  Workshops for new plot holders\nExperienced members are running four Saturday workshops on soil, sowing, pests and harvesting. Each two-hour session takes place on the demonstration plot, so wear old clothes and boots that you do not mind getting dirty. Workshops cost £3 each, and places are limited to twelve. Sign up on the sheet in the meeting room.\n\nF  Bonfires\nFollowing complaints from the houses along Ash Lane, bonfires are no longer allowed on the site between April and October. In winter, small fires may be lit on weekdays only and must be put out before dark. Garden waste can also be taken to the council's recycling centre on Mill Road, which accepts it free of charge."},{"title":"Millfield Community Garden: information for new members","kind":"garden rules","body":"Millfield Community Garden is run entirely by volunteers and is open to anyone who lives in the Millfield area. Please read the points below before your first visit.\n\nMembership\nMembership costs £12 a year, or £6 for students and people over 65. Members receive a key to the main gate and can visit at any time between 7 am and 8 pm. Children are welcome, but they must be with an adult at all times.\n\nShared beds and individual beds\nMost of the garden is made up of shared beds, which all members look after together. Produce from these beds is divided among the members who worked on them, and anything left over is passed on to the food bank on Hill Street. A small number of individual beds are available for members who would like to grow their own crops. These are allocated each March, and there is usually a waiting list.\n\nWork days\nGroup work days take place on the first and third Saturday of every month, from 10 am to 2 pm. All members are asked to come to at least one work day a month, although we understand that this is not always possible. Lunch is provided.\n\nTools\nTools are kept in the green shed and may be used by any member, but they must not be taken out of the garden. Please report any damage to a committee member.\n\nWhat we do not allow\nTo protect wildlife and the soil, chemical weedkillers and pesticides may not be used anywhere in the garden. Dogs are not permitted, with the exception of assistance dogs.\n\nGetting involved\nThe committee meets every two months, and all members are welcome to attend. If you have an idea for a new project or event, you can also leave a note in the suggestions box by the shed."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 1-7. Look at the six notices, A-F, on the Ashgrove Allotments noticeboard. Which notice mentions the following? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"match","prompt":"a rule introduced after people living nearby complained","correct":5,"evidence":"Following complaints from the houses along Ash Lane","why":{"en":"F: \"Following complaints from the houses along Ash Lane\": people living nearby = the houses along the lane.","tr":"F: \"Ash Lane boyunca sıralanan evlerden gelen şikâyetlerin ardından\": people living nearby = the houses along the lane.","fa":"⁨F⁩: «پس از شکایت خانه‌های کنار ⁨Ash Lane⁩»: یعنی کسانی که نزدیک آن‌جا زندگی می‌کنند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":2,"kind":"match","prompt":"a cost that was much higher than predicted","correct":1,"evidence":"our water bill was more than twice what we had expected","why":{"en":"B: the water bill \"was more than twice what we had expected\". E also mentions a cost, but not a higher one.","tr":"B: su faturası \"beklediğimizin iki katından fazlaydı\". E de bir ücretten söz ediyor ama beklenenden yüksek bir ücretten değil.","fa":"⁨B⁩: قبض آب «بیش از دو برابر چیزی بود که انتظار داشتیم». ⁨E⁩ هم از هزینه حرف می‌زند، اما نه هزینه‌ای بیشتر از انتظار."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-samewords"]},{"n":3,"kind":"match","prompt":"someone who has more land than they can look after","correct":2,"evidence":"I can no longer manage all of it","why":{"en":"C: Rita \"can no longer manage all of it\": look after = manage.","tr":"C: Rita \"artık hepsiyle ilgilenemiyor\": look after = manage.","fa":"⁨C⁩: ریتا «دیگر نمی‌تواند به همه‌اش برسد»: ⁨look after⁩ یعنی ⁨manage⁩."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":4,"kind":"match","prompt":"items that must have their names written on them","correct":0,"evidence":"envelopes labelled with the name of the plant","why":{"en":"A: seeds go in \"envelopes labelled with the name of the plant\".","tr":"A: tohumlar \"üzerinde bitkinin adı yazılı zarflarda\" olmalı.","fa":"⁨A⁩: بذرها باید در «پاکت‌هایی باشند که اسم گیاه رویشان نوشته شده»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":5,"kind":"match","prompt":"a limit on how long something can be borrowed","correct":3,"evidence":"for up to three days at a time","why":{"en":"D: tools can be borrowed \"for up to three days at a time\". B limits the hours of the taps, not borrowing.","tr":"D: aletler \"bir seferde en fazla üç gün\" ödünç alınabilir. B musluk saatlerini sınırlıyor, ödünç almayı değil.","fa":"⁨D⁩: ابزارها را می‌شود «هر بار حداکثر سه روز» قرض گرفت. ⁨B⁩ ساعت باز بودن شیرها را محدود می‌کند، نه قرض گرفتن را."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-samewords"]},{"n":6,"kind":"match","prompt":"advice about what to wear","correct":4,"evidence":"wear old clothes and boots","why":{"en":"E: \"wear old clothes and boots that you do not mind getting dirty\".","tr":"E: \"kirlenmesini dert etmeyeceğin eski kıyafetler ve botlar giy\".","fa":"⁨E⁩: «لباس‌های کهنه و چکمه‌هایی بپوش که کثیف شدنشان برایت مهم نیست»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":7,"kind":"match","prompt":"another way to get rid of plant waste","correct":5,"evidence":"Garden waste can also be taken to the council's recycling centre","why":{"en":"F again: garden waste \"can also be taken to the council's recycling centre\". F is used twice.","tr":"Yine F: bahçe atıkları \"belediyenin geri dönüşüm merkezine de götürülebilir\". F iki kez kullanılıyor.","fa":"باز هم ⁨F⁩: زباله‌ی باغچه را «می‌شود به مرکز بازیافت شهرداری هم برد». ⁨F⁩ دو بار به کار می‌رود."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-samewords"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 8-14. Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":8,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Students pay less than the standard membership fee.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"£6 for students and people over 65","why":{"en":"Membership is £12, \"or £6 for students\": less than the standard fee.","tr":"Üyelik 12 £, \"öğrenciler için 6 £\": standart ücretten az.","fa":"عضویت ۱۲ پوند است «یا ۶ پوند برای دانشجوها»: کمتر از هزینه‌ی معمولی."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":9,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Members may visit the garden at any hour of the day or night.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"can visit at any time between 7 am and 8 pm","why":{"en":"Members can visit \"at any time between 7 am and 8 pm\", not at night.","tr":"Üyeler \"sabah 7 ile akşam 8 arasında istedikleri zaman\" gelebilir, gece değil.","fa":"عضوها «هر وقت بین ساعت ۷ صبح تا ۸ شب» می‌توانند بیایند، نه نیمه‌شب."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords"]},{"n":10,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Food that members do not take is given away.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"anything left over is passed on to the food bank on Hill Street","why":{"en":"\"Anything left over is passed on to the food bank\": given away = passed on.","tr":"\"Artan her şey gıda bankasına verilir\": given away = passed on.","fa":"«هر چه اضافه بماند به بانک غذا داده می‌شود»: ⁨given away⁩ یعنی ⁨passed on⁩."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":11,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Members pay extra to have an individual bed.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"A small number of individual beds are available","why":{"en":"Individual beds are allocated each March, but nothing is said about a fee.","tr":"Bireysel tarhlar her mart ayında dağıtılıyor ama ücretten hiç söz edilmiyor.","fa":"کرت‌های شخصی هر سال ماه مارس تقسیم می‌شوند، اما از هزینه حرفی نیست."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":12,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Lunch on work days is paid for by the council.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"Lunch is provided","why":{"en":"\"Lunch is provided\", but the text does not say who pays for it.","tr":"\"Öğle yemeği veriliyor\" ama metin bunu kimin ödediğini söylemiyor.","fa":"«ناهار داده می‌شود»، اما متن نمی‌گوید هزینه‌اش را چه کسی می‌دهد."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords"]},{"n":13,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Members may take the garden tools home.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"they must not be taken out of the garden","why":{"en":"Tools \"must not be taken out of the garden\".","tr":"Aletler \"bahçenin dışına çıkarılmamalı\".","fa":"ابزارها «نباید از باغ بیرون برده شوند»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":14,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"No dogs of any kind are allowed in the garden.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"with the exception of assistance dogs","why":{"en":"Dogs are not permitted \"with the exception of assistance dogs\", so some dogs are allowed.","tr":"Köpekler \"yardımcı köpekler hariç\" yasak; yani bazı köpeklere izin var.","fa":"سگ‌ها ممنوع‌اند «به‌جز سگ‌های کمکی»، پس بعضی سگ‌ها اجازه‌ی ورود دارند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]}]}],"id":"c-x11-r1-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Individual beds are allocated each March.\" Allocated means...","options":["given out to people","sold at a higher price","dug and prepared"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Allocate = give something to particular people for them to use.","tr":"Allocate = bir şeyi belirli kişilere kullanmaları için vermek.","fa":"⁨allocate⁩ یعنی چیزی را برای استفاده به افراد مشخصی دادن."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A question says \"has more land than they can look after\". Which words in a notice mean the same?","options":["can no longer manage all of it","would pay half of the annual rent","has a small shed and two fruit bushes"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Cannot manage all of it = has more than they can look after.","tr":"Hepsiyle ilgilenemiyor = bakabileceğinden fazlası var.","fa":"«نمی‌تواند به همه‌اش برسد» یعنی بیشتر از توانش زمین دارد."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Seven questions and six notices (A-F). What does this tell you?","options":["At least one letter is used twice","One notice is not used","Every letter is used once"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Seven answers from six letters: at least one letter must repeat.","tr":"Altı harften yedi cevap: En az bir harf tekrar etmeli.","fa":"هفت جواب از شش حرف: دست‌کم یک حرف باید تکرار شود."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Refreshments are served at the meeting.\" Statement: \"Refreshments at the meeting are free.\"","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The text says refreshments are served, but not whether they cost anything.","tr":"Metin ikram yapıldığını söylüyor ama ücretli olup olmadığını söylemiyor.","fa":"متن می‌گوید پذیرایی هست، اما نمی‌گوید پولی است یا نه."}}],"id":"c-x11-r1-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r1"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
